  "brice2021": {
   "title": "Brice et al. (2021), PCI Journal May-June 2021, appendix Table A.10 (Ohio DOT standard girders)",
   "local_path": "sources/expansion/round2/us/pcij-2021-mj-brice-appendix.pdf",
   "pdf_page": "Table A.10"
  }
 },
 "geometry_notes": [
  "Outlines are the CAD concrete-outline lines of the PSID-1-13 sections (sheet 1: weight-2 lines on levels 4/5; sheets 2-3: level 7), polygonised with shapely and scaled at 1250 UOR = 1 in (confirmed by the drawn 18 in Type II soffit and every section's depth). All vertices round to 1/16 in with residual <0.0005 in; every outline is symmetric.",
  "Soffit corners are 3/4 in chamfers in the CAD geometry (callout '3/4\" CHAMFER (TYP.)').",
  "Gross concrete only; flange clipping (max 6 in) and shipping holes are not modelled."
 ],
 "discrepancies": [
  "PSID-1-13 printed A/yb/I for Types II, III, IV and Modified IV 60/66 are those of the section WITHOUT the 3/4 in soffit chamfers (difference 2 x 0.28 in2 and ~0.5625*yb^2 in4); the chamfered CAD outline reproduces them exactly when the chamfers are squared off. Modified IV 72 printed values match the chamfered outline.",
  "PSID-1-13 printed WF areas are 0.4 in2 (0.04%) larger and I 53-339 in4 (<=0.06%) larger than the chamfered CAD outline; Brice et al. (2021) Table A.10 matches the CAD outline exactly (A, Ix, Iy to all printed digits)."
 ],
 "provenance": "transcribed",
